From f7fb8a55e61b1ce40929b78945975c9c6a50472b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takumi Ando <takumi@spacecubics.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:45:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: Validate compatible and add an sf probe
 override

Validate a named device against its RDID instead of selecting a different
part. Preserve auto-detection for generic or unspecified compatibles.

Make validation and the recovery override opt-in through
SPI_FLASH_VALIDATE_COMPAT. Leave automatic RDID detection unchanged when
the option is disabled.

Add sf probe --trust-compat for recovery using a known named part without
initial RDID validation. Keep the request per device and clear it after
each command, including failed probes. Use the named manufacturer for the
boot-time reset and the already selected part during removal so recovery
does not depend on a preliminary RDID read. Propagate removal-time
reset failures.

Preserve the original probe error when an explicit speed or mode is given,
just as when device-tree defaults are used.

Signed-off-by: Takumi Ando <takumi@spacecubics.com>
---
 arch/sandbox/include/asm/test.h |  14 ++
 cmd/sf.c                        |  54 +++--
 drivers/mtd/spi/Kconfig         |  15 ++
 drivers/mtd/spi/sandbox.c       |  19 ++
 drivers/mtd/spi/sf-uclass.c     |  36 +++-
 drivers/mtd/spi/sf_probe.c      |   9 +-
 drivers/mtd/spi/spi-nor-core.c  | 115 +++++++++--
 include/spi_flash.h             |  23 +++
 test/dm/sf.c                    | 339 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 9 files changed, 589 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/sandbox/include/asm/test.h b/arch/sandbox/include/asm/test.h
